    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nREA Dawson are delighted to present to the market this exceptional residential farm extending to approximately 162.54 acres (65.78 hectares), all contained within one substantial and well-balanced block.\n\nThe property represents an outstanding agricultural holding, combining quality lands, an attractive and highly productive layout, an extensive range of farm buildings and a distinguished Georgian-style period residence.\n\nThe lands are predominantly laid out in permanent pasture and are divided into a number of large, well-proportioned and easily managed fields, providing an excellent grazing platform and offering considerable versatility for a range of agricultural enterprises. The compact nature of the holding, together with the quality of the lands and extensive farmyard facilities, makes this an extremely attractive proposition for both established farming enterprises and purchasers seeking to acquire a substantial standalone holding.\n\nThe farm is further enhanced by a traditional farmyard with an extensive range of agricultural buildings, together with a number of attractive stone-built outbuildings. The combination of the quality lands, extensive buildings and private residential accommodation creates a highly desirable and versatile agricultural property.\n\n \n\nThe Property\n\nThe holding extends to approximately 162.54 acres (65.78 hectares) and is contained within one compact block, an important feature which provides excellent convenience for farming and day-to-day management.\n\nThe lands are currently in permanent pasture and are divided into large fields, with a layout that lends itself particularly well to grazing and livestock farming. The holding offers scope for a variety of agricultural enterprises including tillage production and provides a substantial land base with excellent potential for further development and improvement.\n\nThe farmyard is strategically positioned within the holding and is serviced by an extensive range of traditional and modern agricultural buildings, providing excellent facilities for farming operations, machinery storage, livestock accommodation and general agricultural use.\n\nA number of traditional stone-built buildings add considerable character to the farmyard and complement the historic nature of the residence.\n\n \n\nThe Residence\n\nSet within the farm is an impressive mid-18th century Georgian-style period residence, approached by a sweeping tree-lined avenue and occupying a private position within the holding.\n\nThe house extends to approximately . sq. m. and is arranged over four levels, including a basement. Constructed of traditional stone with a rendered exterior beneath a natural slate roof, the residence displays elegant proportions and a wealth of period character.\n\nInternally, the house retains a number of original architectural features and offers generous accommodation throughout. While requiring modernisation, the residence provides a unique opportunity to sympathetically restore a substantial period country house and create an impressive family home overlooking the surrounding farm.\n\nThe residence is an important and attractive component of the holding; however, it is the scale, quality and compact nature of the agricultural lands, together with the extensive farmyard facilities, that make this property particularly noteworthy.\n\nThe Accommodation Comprises\n\nMain Hallway 3.5 x 9.4 with timber floor, landing, coving centre piece in ceiling\n\nReception Room 5.1 x 5.8 with marble fireplace, timber floor\n\nDining Room 5.0 x 5.7 with black marble fireplace, timber floor, cornice centre piece\n\nKitchen 5.7 x 2.4 with fitted units, oil fired aga\n\nDownstairs wc whb \n\nStorage Room No. 1 2.4 x 3.4\n\nStorage Room No. 2 2.4 x 2.0\n\nFirst Floor Landing\n\nBedroom No. 1 4.2 x 5.4 with timber floor, cast iron fireplace Dressing Room 2.0 x 2.4\n\nBedroom No. 2 4.2 x 3.5 with timber floor\n\nBedroom No. 3 4.2 x 5.1 \n\nBedroom No. 4 \n\nFamily Bathroom 2.2 x 2.3 with bath, wc, whb, fully tiled\n\nSecond Floor\n\nBedroom No. 5 5.2 x 5.6 with timber floor\n\nAttic Room off 2.4 x 2.6 \n\nBedroom No. 6 5.6 x 5.6 with cast iron fireplace\n\nRoom 2.4 x 5.7\n\nBasement - Selection of storage rooms including\n\nUtility / wash area 4.1 x 6.2 with sink unit\n\nStorage Room No. 1 4.3 x 3.6\n\nBoiler Room 5.0 x 2.0\n\nStorage Room No. 2 1.9 x 3.8\n\nStorage Room No. 3 2.9 x 5.2 \n\n \n\nLocation\n\nThe property enjoys an excellent rural location just off the L8099 BallyragganPhilpstown Road, immediately south of the Kildare/Carlow border.\n\nThe holding is situated approximately:\n\n5 km from Rathvilly\n\n8 km from Castledermot, Co. Kildare\n\n11 km from Baltinglass, Co. Wicklow\n\n14 km from Tullow, Co. Carlow\n\n41 km from Blessington\n\n88 km from Dublin City Centre\n\nThe property is also conveniently located close to the N80 DublinTullowWexford Road, providing excellent access to Dublin and the southeast.\n\nThe surrounding area is well known for its strong agricultural tradition, while the nearby towns of Rathvilly, Castledermot, Tullow and Baltinglass provide a comprehensive range of services and amenities.\n\n \n\nA Substantial Agricultural Holding\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial residential farm extending to approximately 162.54 acres, all contained within one compact block and complemented by an extensive range of agricultural buildings and a distinguished period residence.\n\nThe quality and layout of the lands, substantial farmyard and residential accommodation, make this a particularly attractive agricultural holding with significant long-term potential.\n\nWhether acquired as an addition to an existing farming enterprise, as a standalone livestock farm or as a substantial rural estate, the property offers a combination of land, buildings, residence and location rarely available in one holding.\n\nFurther details, maps and information on the individual lots are available from REA Dawson\n\nViewing strictly by prior appointment with auctioneer\n\n"
      }
